    "introduction": "British American Tobacco manufactures and markets tobacco and nicotine products through an international distribution network. Its portfolio includes cigarette brands such as Dunhill, Lucky Strike and Pall Mall, alongside Vuse vapour products, glo heated products and Velo nicotine pouches. Revenue comes from repeat purchases of consumable products, with pricing, brand choice and retail availability influencing demand. The group is developing newer nicotine categories while managing its established cigarette operations. Its economics are shaped by excise duties, product regulation, marketing restrictions and changes in consumer behaviour. Manufacturing consistency and distribution scale matter, as does the ability to compete across markets with very different legal frameworks.",
